# Rule: skill invocation and agent routing

Cursor has no `context: fork` field. Isolation is a Task (subagent) spawn: a fresh prompt, no
prior conversation history, and a summary back to the main loop. Choosing Task versus staying
inline makes skills slow, lossy, or unsafe if it is wrong.

## The rule

- **Stay in the main loop** when ANY hold: it is a gated, mutating workflow (commit, rebase, push,
  tag, admin-merge) that needs main-loop visibility and confirmations; it is a knowledge-injection
  skill whose whole purpose is to enrich the MAIN context (`session-lifecycle`, `cross-platform`,
  `ipc-bridge`, `debug-activity`); it is active implementation tied to the current conversation;
  or it is spawned as an incidental side-check while a gated/mutating skill remains active in the
  same conversation. An ambiguous prompt can cause a subagent to complete the skill's remaining
  steps independently (this shipped a duplicate PR during `pull-request`). `test` and `sync-docs`
  stay inline for this reason.
- **Delegate with Task** for heavy, self-contained judgment that should not pollute the main
  session: `add-ipc-endpoint` to `ipc-auditor`, `add-migration` to `migration-safety`, and
  `code-review` to its dimension auditors (`ipc-auditor`, `hmr-parity`, `platform-guard`,
  `session-debugger`, `migration-safety`) fanned out as parallel in-session subagents and
  synthesized in the main loop. `test` delegates to `test-builder` for coverage audits and test
  writing in a single in-session pass; `code-review` likewise delegates coverage-hole test-writing
  to `test-builder` in its Apply Phase, so `test-builder` stays the single source of truth for
  tier classification.
- **Gated mutating skills** (`commit`, `pull-request`, `merge-pull-request`, `merge-back`,
  `release`, `release-protocol`, `test`, `preview`, `sentry`, `code-review`) set
  `disable-model-invocation: true` so they run only when named. Knowledge skills omit that field
  so the agent can pull them in from the description.
- **Read-only auditor agents** set `readonly: true`. Agents that write tests or capture assets
  (`test-builder`, `marketing-captures`) set `readonly: false`. Cursor has no per-tool allowlist.
  Use `model: inherit` unless a specific model ID is required.
- **Cursor does not preload skills from agent frontmatter.** An auditor whose Claude copy used
  `skills:` must Read the matching `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` in its body.
- **Never route a fixing or mutating skill to `explore`.** That built-in subagent is read-only and
  drops project conventions (no em-dashes, no `any`). Keep mutating work on the default agent or
  a project subagent that loads `AGENTS.md`.

## Enforcement (self-maintaining)

- **Review:** judgment-based, applied when authoring or editing a skill or agent. No mechanical
  test - skill routing is a design decision, not a code shape.

## Scope

Skill and agent authoring under `.cursor/`. Does not govern product code. The `.claude/` copies
stay for Claude Code sessions and for the product's agent spawn path.
